rem Polynomials with at Least One
rem Integer Root
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=269
rem Count the n up to 10^K whose digits,
rem taken as the coefficients of a
rem polynomial, give one with an integer
rem root

use bits
use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg K integer = 16

rem The roots can only be 0 and -1 to
rem -9. Root 0 is a last digit 0, and
rem 10^K is one of these n. For the
rem others, by inclusion and exclusion
rem over sets S of roots, count the
rem digit strings with last digit 1 to 9
rem whose polynomial P is divisible by
rem G, the product of x + r for r in S.
rem Dividing from the low end, P = G Q
rem gives q[i] = (p[i] - sum g[j]
rem q[i-j]) / g[0] so the state is the
rem last d quotient coefficients, d the
rem degree of G, packed in base B.
rem For the last d digits q[i] must be
rem zero: Q has degree less than K-d.
rem Equal states merge by sort.
Base = 2001
Off = 1000
Total = 10 ** (K - 1)
Zero = array 0
Pos = 0 to 8 array
for Mask in 1 to 511
  Sel' = (Mask shr Pos) band 1 equal 1
  Rs = (1 to 9 array) filter Sel array
  rem G[0] must divide the last digit.
  if (Rs reduce *) greater 9
    continue
  end
  G = array 1
  for R in Rs
    Up' = concat G Zero
    Sh' = concat Zero G
    G = Up * R + Sh
  end
  D = G len - 1
  Lead = G 0
  Gw = G drop 1
  Pw = Base ** (0 to (D - 1) array)
  Key0 = ((Pw - Pw + Off) * Pw) sum
  Keep = Base ** (D - 1)
  Keys = array Key0
  Cnts = array 1
  for I in 0 till K
    N = Keys len
    if N equal 0
      break
    end
    Col = Keys reshape N 1
    Lag = (Col // Pw) mod Base - Off
    Back = (Lag * Gw) sum axis 1
    Tail = Keys mod Keep
    Lo = 0
    Hi = 9
    if I equal 0
      Lo = 1
    end
    rem Digits form rows, states columns.
    Width = Hi - Lo + 1
    Digits = (Lo to Hi array) reshape Width 1
    Acc = Digits - Back
    Q = Acc // Lead
    Fit = Acc mod Lead equal 0
    Fit = Fit and (Q at most Off - 1)
    Fit = Fit and (Q at least 1 - Off)
    if I at least K - D
      Fit = Fit and (Q equal 0)
    end
    Cells = Width * N
    Masked = Fit reshape Cells
    Next' = ((Q + Off) + Base * Tail) reshape Cells
    Counts' = (Cnts + Digits * 0) reshape Cells
    NK = Next filter Masked array
    NC = Counts filter Masked array
    Keys = NK
    Cnts = NC
    if Keys len equal 0
      break
    end
    Ord = Keys argsort
    Ks = Keys Ord
    Cum = (Cnts Ord) scan +
    Tl = Ks drop 1
    Nx = concat Tl (array -1)
    Last = Ks not equal Nx
    Ke = Ks filter Last array
    Ce = Cum filter Last array
    H = Ke len
    Hd = Ce take (H - 1)
    Pc = concat Zero Hd
    Keys = Ke
    Cnts = Ce - Pc
  end
  Hit = Keys equal Key0
  Done = Cnts filter Hit
  Count = Done sum
  Sign = 1 - 2 * ((Rs len + 1) mod 2)
  Total += Sign * Count
end
Answer = Total
Answer print
